      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2743425c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a photo of actor Christopher Lee with overlaid text reading \"i'll take shit that ain't ever gonna happen for $500.\" The meme uses Lee's serious, slightly amused facial expression to mock the absurdity of someone agreeing to take a ridiculous or impossible deal for a small amount of money. The intent is humorous and satirical, aiming to highlight the irrationality or desperation of the situation being described. While the text contains vulgar language, it does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics (race, gender, religion, etc.) and is not abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful. The meme's overall intent is to entertain through absurdity and irony, not to cause harm or promote hate. The harmfulness, if any, is minimal and stems from the crude language, which may be offensive to some but does not constitute targeted toxicity against any community.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f2df3567"
      },
